          mainEntity: [
          {
                    "@type": "Question",
                    "name": "What does a custom web development company actually do?",
                    "acceptedAnswer": {
                              "@type": "Answer",
                              "text": "A custom web development company designs, engineers, and deploys websites and web applications built around a specific business's requirements — rather than adapting those requirements to a pre-built template or platform. A serious custom web development engagement covers architecture planning, UI/UX design, frontend and backend engineering, database design, security implementation, third-party integrations, and — in 2026 — the structured data, schema markup, and rendering decisions that determine whether the site is visible in traditional search and AI-generated answers from day one."
                    }
          },
          {
                    "@type": "Question",
                    "name": "What is the difference between custom web development and using a website builder?",
                    "acceptedAnswer": {
                              "@type": "Answer",
                              "text": "A website builder constrains the site to the platform's template system, plugin ecosystem, and hosting infrastructure — limiting what can be built, how it performs, and how it integrates with other systems. Custom web development produces a site built specifically for one business, carrying only the code it needs, owned entirely by the client, and architecturally positioned to accommodate future features without rebuilding the foundation. The performance and visibility gap between the two widens as the business grows beyond what the template was designed to accommodate."
                    }
          },
          {
                    "@type": "Question",
                    "name": "How does custom web development affect SEO and AI search visibility?",
                    "acceptedAnswer": {
                              "@type": "Answer",
                              "text": "Significantly — because the most consequential SEO and AI visibility decisions are architectural choices made at build time, not optimization tasks applied after launch. Rendering strategy determines whether AI platforms can parse the site's content without executing JavaScript. Schema markup built into the component architecture ensures every new page automatically inherits correct structured data. Core Web Vitals performance engineered at build time avoids the remediation cost and ranking penalty of a slow site discovered after launch. Custom web development is the only context in which these decisions can be made correctly the first time."
                    }
          },
          {
                    "@type": "Question",
                    "name": "What industries particularly benefit from custom web development?",
                    "acceptedAnswer": {
                              "@type": "Answer",
                              "text": "Healthcare, fintech, B2B, and e-commerce benefit most — each carries compliance requirements (HIPAA, PCI DSS, GDPR), integration complexity (EHR systems, payment rails, CRM pipelines), or performance demands at scale that template platforms consistently fail to accommodate as the business grows. Any business where the website is a primary revenue or lead generation channel, rather than a basic informational presence, benefits from the architectural control that custom development provides."
                    }
          }
]
