          '@type': 'FAQPage',
          '@id': 'https://www.abuqitmirlabs.tech/blog/local-seo-checklist-2026-audit-citations-pricing-industry-guide#faq',
          mainEntity: [
          {
                    "@type": "Question",
                    "name": "What should be included in a local SEO checklist?",
                    "acceptedAnswer": {
                              "@type": "Answer",
                              "text": "A complete local SEO checklist covers Google Business Profile optimization (complete NAP data, service descriptions, regular photos and posts), citation building and consistency across directories, review generation and response management, on-page local signals (schema markup, location pages, local keyword usage), and local link building from community and industry sources. Businesses should audit these areas quarterly at minimum, since profile freshness and citation accuracy both decay over time without maintenance."
                    }
          },
          {
                    "@type": "Question",
                    "name": "How much does local SEO cost?",
                    "acceptedAnswer": {
                              "@type": "Answer",
                              "text": "Local SEO cost depends on business size, market competitiveness, and number of locations. Single-location small businesses typically pay the least; competitive industries like legal and healthcare in dense markets require more investment; multi-location and franchise local SEO is usually priced per location given the scale of consistency management required. A credible local SEO specialist explains what specifically a package includes rather than quoting a single opaque fee."
                    }
          },
          {
                    "@type": "Question",
                    "name": "What is white-label local SEO?",
                    "acceptedAnswer": {
                              "@type": "Answer",
                              "text": "White-label local SEO is a service where an agency resells fully managed local SEO — audits, citation building, GBP management, and reporting — to its own clients under its own brand, while a specialized provider handles the actual execution behind the scenes. It allows web design agencies and marketing firms to offer local SEO without building in-house expertise."
                    }
          },
          {
                    "@type": "Question",
                    "name": "How is local SEO different for franchises and multi-location businesses?",
                    "acceptedAnswer": {
                              "@type": "Answer",
                              "text": "Local SEO for franchises requires managing consistent NAP data, accurate individual Google Business Profiles, and citation accuracy across every location simultaneously. Inconsistency across locations directly undermines rankings for all of them, which makes centralized management and regular auditing essential at scale in a way single-location businesses don't need to worry about."
                    }
          },
          {
                    "@type": "Question",
                    "name": "Why is Google Business Profile so important for local SEO?",
                    "acceptedAnswer": {
                              "@type": "Answer",
                              "text": "Google Business Profile functions as a free digital storefront that often reaches searchers before they ever visit a business's website. A complete, regularly updated profile with accurate information, service descriptions, and fresh photos directly affects both traditional local pack rankings and — increasingly in 2026 — whether a business gets surfaced in Google's AI-generated local answers, since AI systems draw heavily on GBP data and structured information rather than website copy alone."
                    }
          },
          {
                    "@type": "Question",
                    "name": "Do local SEO tactics still matter with AI Overviews appearing in more searches?",
                    "acceptedAnswer": {
                              "@type": "Answer",
                              "text": "Yes, arguably more than before. AI Overviews and AI-generated local recommendations draw on the same underlying signals as traditional local SEO — structured data, Google Business Profile completeness, citation consistency, and review volume. Businesses with strong, consistent local SEO foundations are the ones AI systems have reliable data to recommend; businesses with thin or inconsistent local presence become harder for both traditional search and AI systems to surface confidently."
                    }
          }
]
